A block opener indented under a definition term is term text at every depth

```
:: c
  # H
.
<dl>
  <dt>c
  # H</dt>
</dl>
```

```
:: c
  ::: note
  body
  :::
.
<dl>
  <dt>c
  ::: note
  body
  :::</dt>
</dl>
```

```
> :: c
>   # H
.
<blockquote>
  <dl>
    <dt>c
  # H</dt>
  </dl>
</blockquote>
```

```
- item

  :: c
    # H
.
<ul>
  <li>item
    <dl>
      <dt>c
  # H</dt>
    </dl>
  </li>
</ul>
```

```
:: a
: b
  :: c
    # H
.
<dl>
  <dt>a</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>b</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>c
  # H</dt>
    </dl>
  </dd>
</dl>
```

```
:: a
: b
  :: c
    ::: note
    body
    :::
.
<dl>
  <dt>a</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>b</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>c
  ::: note
  body
  :::</dt>
    </dl>
  </dd>
</dl>
```

```
:: c
# H
.
<dl>
  <dt>c</dt>
</dl>
<section id="H">
  <h1>H</h1>
</section>
```

```
:: a
: b
  :: c
  # H
.
<dl>
  <dt>a</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>b</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>c</dt>
    </dl>
    <h1 id="H">H</h1>
  </dd>
</dl>
```

```
:: a
: b
  :: c
    - x
.
<dl>
  <dt>a</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>b</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>c</dt>
    </dl>
    <ul>
      <li>x</li>
    </ul>
  </dd>
</dl>
```

```
:: c
::: note
body
:::
.
<dl>
  <dt>c</dt>
</dl>
<aside class="admonition note" aria-label="Note">
  <p>body</p>
</aside>
```
